 {:db/id "q-176865" :question/id #uuid "9b8bbb71-5c94-5fce-b0d2-f79d72a9b4c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-176865" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is a rational number}$\n\n- $Q:-2\\text{ is negative}$" :question/worked-solution "The sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∨Q.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-176865/ma-source-field/c7ebd3dd29aeff04c1715c78ec785028311403a823d4e82f5852c39c8cd7e166"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
