 {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffbf219-9fc7-55d4-a011-546b8183375e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/e336f34dbaf1fa6f82e0085208e000e22d99dead9bb6ec9bacc47968aa86e62a" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/d1014c3b89fa16147087f3cf34ee892fe2126f1cb5b8e3d8e0e6d07671c9b099" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/6752e17097f799416eda38d375be7f7edefdcdefa1bac5adb4a5dc8f8b29e5c1" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/0a3f2fdc622369df0cd849230eedcd4b4cb11f46733e1d2af9c3fcca69fc319c" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/5a65408d9c616b2430efb0c8cb2ab532728ae3bcdab95c0e7dd032f37f6dd1b3"] :answer-field/correct "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/e336f34dbaf1fa6f82e0085208e000e22d99dead9bb6ec9bacc47968aa86e62a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "fee02912-87a3-5a99-92ba-f8ae9f270c88"] :question/problem "The equations of a curve $r(t)$ and its corresponding unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at an arbitrary point are given below. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at the point $P(0,3,4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ) \\\\ T(t) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,3,4)$ on the given curve. We know that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,3,4⟩ \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+3\\text{ }j+4\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components of $i$, $j$, and $k$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=3 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,3,4)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,3,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=\\frac{-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k}{1}=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =(-i)\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(i\\cdot j)+\\frac{4}{5}(i\\cdot k) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
