 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ecd4b4f8-b1ae-5164-9bed-1e7df536d7e1"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334329/ma-source-field/2ed981a740beb0274bff73582ff8d8b5299c1dfcae6c71e62d58b33ca37d01dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
